== strategist
use: strategist
short: Strategist skill CLI
long: |
  Strategist — install, compile, and manage the Strategist skill for Claude agents.

== strategist check
use: check
short: Pre-mission slot validation
long: |
  Validate that slot providers declared in active.yaml are installed and
  satisfy their risk_score contracts.
  
  Checks performed:
    - active.yaml is present and parseable
    - For each slot (discovery, refinement, execution):
        • plugins/catalog.yaml or a bound custom provider resolves the Weapon, OR
          roles/<provider>.yaml exists with matching slot field (native role)
        • cataloged Weapons and bound custom providers must declare the correct risk_score for the slot contract:
          discovery/refinement → write_analysis, execution → controlled
        • native roles are accepted by slot field match; no risk_score check
    - discovery and refinement must have one valid persisted weapon binding in plugins.lock
    - role affinity and active.yaml/plugins.lock parity are validated fail-closed
flag: --confirm-chat-language (string) default="" usage="acknowledge the chat language the invoking agent read and intends to use; if it does not match active.yaml's language.chat, check fails with warning=chat_language_mismatch instead of silently drifting"
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="print one domain.PreflightResult JSON object ({schema_version, status, identity, bindings, language, warnings, next}) instead of the human-readable banner; does not run missions or mutate mission state; ranked providers may run their own healthcheck command, which can create provider-home directories under the runtime root"
flag: --persona (string) default="" usage="persona/mode to read with --print-content-by-lang (default: active.yaml's mode)"
flag: --print-content-by-lang (string) default="" usage="print personas.<persona>.content_by_lang.<lang> and phase_announcements.<lang> from the compiled artifact as JSON and exit; use this instead of reading persona YAML directly to resolve non-English chat templates and mission narration lines"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"
flag: --simulate (bool) default="false" usage="print a readiness report (per-slot/persona status) instead of the pass/fail banner; does not run missions or mutate mission state; ranked providers may run their own healthcheck command, which can create provider-home directories under the runtime root"
flag: --strict (bool) default="false" usage="additionally require compiled artifacts to exist and match the recorded manifest hashes"

== strategist check-stale
use: check-stale <artifact.gz>
short: Check if a compiled artifact is stale (exit 0=fresh, exit 1=stale)
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="print stale-check result as JSON"
flag: --quiet (bool) default="false" usage="suppress human-readable stale output"

== strategist compile
use: compile
short: Compile all skill artifacts from a .strategist/ root
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist dojo
use: dojo
short: Health-check scenarios for the Strategist skill
long: |
  Dojo validates that Strategist is correctly installed, configured, and operating.
  
  Run a scenario check:
    strategist dojo check <scenario>
  
  List available scenarios:
    strategist dojo list
  
  Calibrate a judge (the provider handoff pre-check) against labeled cases:
    strategist dojo calibrate <case> --dry-run
    strategist dojo calibrate <case> --consent

== strategist dojo audit
use: audit <case>
short: Sample generated negatives for review, or record an audit verdict
long: |
  Without --record, print a deterministic sample of the generated negatives (operator, band, expected
  criteria and the names of the fields that changed; never content) for a reviewer to check. With --record <case-id>
  --verdict agree|disagree, append the verdict to the case's audit log. A disagreement excludes the case from the
  metrics and appears in the lesson; an audit never relabels a case, and a stage 2 case counts only after an agree.
flag: --by (string) default="" usage="reviewer name (with --record)"
flag: --note (string) default="" usage="why, in one sentence (with --record)"
flag: --record (string) default="" usage="case id to record a verdict for"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"
flag: --sample (int) default="10" usage="number of generated negatives to sample"
flag: --verdict (string) default="" usage="agree or disagree (with --record)"

== strategist dojo calibrate
use: calibrate <case>
short: Run a judge calibration case against labeled cases
long: |
  Evaluate a judge (the provider handoff pre-check) against cases whose expected verdict is known,
  keep every raw observation and publish a calibration record. Nothing is trained: the run measures the
  judge and recommends a threshold only when the judge is fit and the sample supports it.
  
    --dry-run    print the exact cases, fields, bytes and estimated usage; no call is made
    --recompute  evaluate the stored observations again, with no call
    --consent    required to send real package fields to the provider
flag: --all-sessions (bool) default="false" usage="with --recompute: use every stored session instead of the latest"
flag: --boundary-margin (float64) default="0" usage="repeat cases whose score is within this margin of the current threshold"
flag: --budget (int) default="0" usage="maximum provider calls for this run (0 means the case's budget)"
flag: --consent (bool) default="false" usage="assent to the consent term: the run calls the external provider"
flag: --consent-term (string) default="" usage="bind the assent to exactly the term id printed by --dry-run; a changed plan is refused"
flag: --dry-run (bool) default="false" usage="print the plan and send nothing"
flag: --exclude-criterion (stringSlice) default="[]" usage="with --recompute: read an atomic profile's stored answers without this criterion (an exploratory what-if over answers already given)"
flag: --exclude-operator (stringSlice) default="[]" usage="with --recompute: leave an operator out of the evaluation (an exploratory what-if, labelled; no calibration is published from it)"
flag: --gate-rule (string) default="" usage="with --recompute: read the observations under gates-1 (the first pilots' rule), gates-2 (default) or gates-3 (cross-validated)"
flag: --judge-only (bool) default="false" usage="with --recompute: ignore the case's delegation to the local checks, so the judge alone answers for every operator (an exploratory what-if)"
flag: --local-scope (stringSlice) default="[]" usage="with --recompute: delegate this operator to the local checks for the evaluation only (an exploratory what-if)"
flag: --recompute (bool) default="false" usage="evaluate the stored observations again with no call"
flag: --repetitions (int) default="0" usage="repetitions per case (0 means the case's value)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist dojo candidate
use: candidate
short: Record a regression candidate from a mission where the provider and the gate disagreed
long: |
  Read a mission's provider readings and its gate outcome and, where they disagreed, record a regression
  candidate (content-free: mission, transition, confidence, outcome). A candidate is only flagged for review; it never
  counts as golden until it is promoted. The DOJO agent never runs this command.
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="mission id (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist dojo check
use: check <scenario>
short: Run offline checks for a dojo scenario
flag: --files-only (bool) default="false" usage="skip checks that require an emit.log run (emit_log, timing, pipeline)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist dojo compare
use: compare <case-a> <case-b>
short: Compare the latest observations of two cases, offline (a laboratory reading)
long: |
  Print, per operator and level, the mean probability of accept of two cases side by side, the AUC
  and an exploratory operating sweep. It reads stored observations only: no call, nothing persisted, no
  calibration and no recommendation. Use it to see what a change of profile or operator set did.
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist dojo corpus
use: corpus <case>
short: List the packages of a case's corpus with an offline screen (no call)
long: |
  List the packages the corpus of <case> would use, with their label and the result of the deterministic
  local checks (missing fields, untyped or unverified tasks, a task type that does not match its action). The screen reads
  files only and never calls a provider. A package with no flag is a candidate for review, not a golden: only
  'strategist dojo promote', a human act, makes it one.
flag: --clean (bool) default="false" usage="list only the packages no local check flags"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist dojo demote
use: demote <case>
short: Withdraw a package from the golden set (a human act)
long: |
  Record that a golden package no longer is: a reviewer and a reason (what in the package does not meet
  the contract) are required. Promotions are append-only, so the demotion is its own record, bound to the package's
  content digest; promoting the same content again makes it golden again. The DOJO agent never runs this command.
flag: --package (string) default="" usage="package name to demote (required)"
flag: --reason (string) default="" usage="what in the package does not meet the contract, in one sentence (required)"
flag: --reviewed-by (string) default="" usage="name of the human reviewer (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist dojo generate
use: generate <case>
short: Write the skeleton of a judge calibration case
long: |
  Write <base_path>/dojo/<case>/criteria.yaml for a judge_calibration case with its defaults and an
  explicit risk policy. The skeleton holds no package content and never overwrites an existing case.
flag: --boundary (string) default="package" usage="boundary to evaluate: package or ranger"
flag: --exclude-operator (stringSlice) default="[]" usage="leave an operator out of the case (recorded in the case and in its calibration)"
flag: --gate-rule (string) default="" usage="gate rule of the case: gates-2 (default) or gates-3 (cross-validated, pre-registered for the real corpus)"
flag: --layer (string) default="judge" usage="judge (the real provider, needs consent), integration (the approval policy against scripted answers, no call) or live (the provider smoke check, needs consent)"
flag: --local-scope (stringSlice) default="[]" usage="delegate this operator's protection to the local checks: the judge gates skip it and a local coverage gate must pass for it"
flag: --package (stringSlice) default="[]" usage="restrict the corpus to this package (repeatable)"
flag: --packages (int) default="8" usage="with --synthetic: how many fixture packages to write (up to 32)"
flag: --profile (string) default="" usage="question profile: handoff-v1 (default), handoff-v2 (a missing field is shown as (absent)) or handoff-atomic-v1 (one question per criterion, the lowest answer decides)"
flag: --repetitions (int) default="0" usage="repetitions per case (0 keeps the default of 3)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"
flag: --synthetic (bool) default="false" usage="write synthetic fixture packages under the case and calibrate over them: golden by construction, nothing real is sent"

== strategist dojo list
use: list
short: List available dojo scenarios
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist dojo promote
use: promote <case>
short: Promote a reviewed package to golden (a human act)
long: |
  Record that a package is a golden positive for the corpus of <case>: a reviewer and an oracle (why it
  is good) are required, and the promotion is bound to the package's content digest, so editing the package
  voids it. The DOJO agent never runs this command.
flag: --oracle (string) default="" usage="why this package is good, in one sentence (required)"
flag: --package (string) default="" usage="package name to promote (required)"
flag: --reviewed-by (string) default="" usage="name of the human reviewer (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist dojo propose
use: propose <operator>
short: Record an operator proposal pending a reviewed change
long: |
  Record a proposal for a new mutation operator under <base_path>/dojo/mutations. It adds nothing to the catalog: a proposal waits for a reviewed change.
flag: --by (string) default="agent" usage="who proposes it"
flag: --description (string) default="" usage="what the operator injects (required)"
flag: --reason (string) default="" usage="which evasion or weak spot motivates it"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist eval
use: eval
short: Strategist eval harness utilities

== strategist eval harvest
use: harvest [mission_id]
short: Copy real mission artifacts into tests/evals/regression/ as fixtures
flag: --all (bool) default="false" usage="harvest every mission found"
flag: --include (string) default="" usage="comma-separated extra artifact types"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist eval run
use: run [pattern]
short: Run the internal/eval scenario battery via go test
flag: --race (bool) default="true" usage="pass -race to go test"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist handoff
use: handoff
short: Run and record Handoff Challenge verification

== strategist handoff criteria
use: criteria
short: Report the quality criteria already computed for a mission (read-only)
long: |
  Prints the quality criteria the Approval Gate shows, gathered only from records earlier
  stages already wrote: route and claim confidence, the confidence review, the deterministic
  handoff outcomes, the critic and mission-quality results, the refinement handoff metrics and
  the provider (JEV) readings, then the token volume per stage (discovery, refining,
  delivering; volumes and their quality only, never cost). Every row is always present and filled: a value, "não avaliado"
  (the stage did not run or was not enabled) or "não sei" (data exists but cannot support a
  statement). The command never calls the provider and never recomputes a criterion.
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="emit machine-readable JSON"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission whose criteria are reported (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist handoff evaluate
use: evaluate
short: Evaluate the Archivist-to-Sniper handoff and record its outcome
long: |
  Evaluates the Archivist-to-Sniper handoff of a mission: validates its refined
  package, derives the policy signals from the package's typed facts, resolves the
  policy, runs the semantic challenge when it is required, and durably records a
  terminal outcome (passed, failed, or a policy-authorized skip) correlated to the
  mission, the package revision and the attempt, and records the handoff confidence
  (or an explicit missing-record). A failed outcome returns the mission to refinement,
  so a repaired package needs a new Approval Gate acceptance; the last allowed failure
  blocks it. A passed or skipped outcome does not enter execution by itself.
  The policy is never chosen by the caller. --risk-level is the optional coarse
  intake label and can only make the result stricter. The Approval Gate must
  already be accepted. Entering execution (mission submit --event
  handoff_challenge_satisfied) verifies and consumes this outcome.
flag: --ack (string) default="" usage="path to an acknowledgment YAML file (needed when the package requires the challenge)"
flag: --challenges (string) default="" usage="path to a challenges YAML file (needed when the package requires the challenge)"
flag: --confidence-summary (string) default="" usage="optional YAML file with the declared handoff confidence_summary; without it a missing-record is written"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission whose Archivist-to-Sniper handoff is evaluated (required)"
flag: --risk-level (string) default="" usage="optional intake risk_level (low, medium, high); can only make the result stricter"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist handoff evaluate-ranger
use: evaluate-ranger
short: Evaluate and persist the Ranger-to-Archivist lifecycle outcome
flag: --ack (string) default="" usage="path to an acknowledgment YAML file when the typed facts require a challenge"
flag: --challenges (string) default="" usage="path to a challenges YAML file when the typed facts require a challenge"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission whose Ranger-to-Archivist handoff is evaluated (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist handoff precheck
use: precheck
short: Read the refined package with the provider before the Approval Gate (advisory)
long: |
  Asks the enabled provider whether the refined package conforms to its contract
  criteria, before the Approval Gate is presented. This is the advisory Archivist to
  Gate boundary: it records no lifecycle outcome and approves nothing. The reading is
  written to the integration call ledger and to the confidence ledger, and the later
  handoff evaluate reuses it when the package digest is unchanged, so the provider is
  not asked twice for one revision. Without an enabled integration it prints
  "delegation: disabled" and changes nothing.
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission whose refined package is read (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist handoff verify
use: verify
short: Verify a Handoff Challenge acknowledgment and record the result
long: |
  Runs internal/handoff.Verify deterministically against a challenges file and
  an acknowledgment file, prints the result, and appends a ChallengeRecord to
  .strategist/memory/handoff-challenges.jsonl.
  
  This gives the LLM agent embodying a Strategist role (Ranger, Archivist,
  Sniper) a scriptable, deterministic tool to invoke instead of reasoning
  through a Handoff Challenge unaided — see docs/architecture/strategist-concepts.md §
  Handoff Challenge "Known Limitations" for why this command exists.
  
  Exits non-zero when verification fails, so callers can gate on it directly.
  This command never authorizes execution. The Archivist-to-Sniper transition is
  decided by 'strategist handoff evaluate', which derives its policy from the
  refined package and records the durable outcome execution entry requires.
flag: --ack (string) default="" usage="path to an acknowledgment YAML file (required)"
flag: --attempt (int) default="1" usage="attempt number, for repair-loop tracking"
flag: --challenges (string) default="" usage="path to a challenges YAML file (required)"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission_id to record against (required)"
flag: --policy (string) default="" usage="path to a policy YAML file, overriding the built-in default for --transition"
flag: --risk-level (string) default="" usage="mission risk_level (low, medium, high) from intake — when set, resolves policy.Enabled/RequiredTypes from risk signals instead of the static per-transition default; ignored if --policy is set"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --transition (string) default="" usage="handoff transition (ranger_to_archivist or sniper_to_validation; archivist_to_sniper is decided by 'handoff evaluate') — ignored if --policy is set"

== strategist install
use: install
short: Install the Strategist skill into a target repository
long: |
  Install the Strategist skill into a target repository.
  
  Silent mode (default, no flags needed) writes epic-profile defaults and never
  prompts. A CompileAll failure after extraction is warning-only by default —
  install still completes with a partial/uncompiled runtime. Pass
  --strict-compile to make that failure fatal (the install rolls back instead).
  
  By default a Claude Code shim is written to
  ~/.claude/skills/strategist/SKILL.md so the skill is invocable outside this
  repository. Use --no-shim to skip that write entirely (e.g. CI/containers
  without a writable home directory), or --shim-path to redirect it.
flag: --allow-downgrade (bool) default="false" usage="let this binary replace normative runtime files installed by a newer binary (deliberate rollback; default: refuse with runtime_newer_than_binary)"
flag: --force (bool) default="false" usage="overwrite all files, including user-modified ones (default: preserve customizations)"
flag: --global (bool) default="false" usage="install into global root (default: local project)"
flag: --integration (string) default="" usage="silent selection for the optional external provider integration: enable, disable or keep (default: no selection; a new install records no decision and an upgrade preserves the existing one)"
flag: --no-shim (bool) default="false" usage="skip writing the SKILL.md shim under ~/.claude/skills (mutually exclusive with --shim-path)"
flag: --shim-path (string) default="" usage="write the SKILL.md shim to this path instead of the default ~/.claude/skills/strategist/SKILL.md (mutually exclusive with --no-shim)"
flag: --silent (bool) default="false" usage="silent install with epic defaults (default)"
flag: --strict-compile (bool) default="false" usage="fail install (and roll back) on a CompileAll error, instead of warning-only (default: warning-only)"
flag: --target (string) default="" usage="target repository root (default: current directory)"
flag: --verbose (bool) default="false" usage="show the INFO log lines, the wizard section headers and the role/provider migration preview that install hides by default"
flag: --wizard (bool) default="false" usage="interactive wizard for configuration"

== strategist integrations
use: integrations
short: Inspect and change the optional external provider integration
long: |
  Manage the optional provider integration (JEV) that pre-checks handoff conformance.
  Strategist works unchanged without it: a provider that is disabled, unreachable or not
  confident enough leaves every handoff on the main path. The operator decision lives in
  .strategist/integrations.yaml; the credential is only a reference (env: or dotenv:) and is
  never stored, printed or sent anywhere but the configured endpoint.

== strategist integrations calibration
use: calibration
short: List, show, pin and unpin the calibration the pre-check threshold follows
long: |
  The approval threshold stays operator configuration. A calibration published by a DOJO case
  (strategist dojo calibrate) is pinned here by id, never "latest": the pre-check uses its threshold only
  while it is valid for the resolved model and the question profile and is not too old, and otherwise
  uses the configured threshold and reports "não calibrado". Nothing pins automatically.

== strategist integrations calibration list
use: list
short: List the published calibrations
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations calibration pin
use: pin <id>
short: Pin a calibration after showing its numbers; --confirm writes the pin
flag: --confirm (bool) default="false" usage="write the pin after reviewing the numbers"
flag: --max-age-days (int) default="0" usage="age limit of the pin in days (0 keeps the default of 90)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations calibration show
use: show [id]
short: Show a calibration with its numbers and risk policy (default: the pinned one)
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations calibration unpin
use: unpin
short: Remove the pin; the configured threshold applies
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations disable
use: disable
short: Record the decision not to use the provider; recorded outcomes and settings are kept
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations doctor
use: doctor
short: Report declared, bound, enabled, compatible and available state without calling the provider
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="emit machine-readable JSON"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations enable
use: enable
short: Record the decision to use the provider (documented defaults, credential stays a reference)
flag: --credential-ref (string) default="" usage="credential reference, env:NAME or dotenv:<path>#NAME (default: dotenv:.env#TYPESAFE_API_KEY)"
flag: --endpoint (string) default="" usage="provider HTTPS endpoint (default: the documented JEV endpoint)"
flag: --model (string) default="" usage="pinned provider model (default: the documented resolved model)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations probe
use: probe
short: Send one synthetic, non-mission message to record availability
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations shadow
use: shadow
short: Keep the provider reading without letting it decide (on, off, report)
long: |
  In shadow mode the pre-check is still called and every reading is recorded in the call ledger together
  with what it would have decided, but no handoff uses it: no delegation, no hint, no confidence claim, and the main
  path decides alone. Use it to collect readings on real missions before a calibration is trusted.
  'shadow report' summarizes the readings (counts and numbers only); to compare one mission's reading with its gate
  outcome run 'strategist dojo candidate --mission <id>'.

== strategist integrations shadow off
use: off
short: Turn shadow mode off (the provider decides again)
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations shadow on
use: on
short: Turn shadow mode on
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist integrations shadow report
use: report
short: Summarize the recorded shadow readings
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist leveling
use: leveling
short: Suggest model and effort by role

== strategist leveling label
use: label
short: Resolve and record the model/effort label shown on a role's log lines
flag: --ambiguity (string) default="" usage="ambiguity signal: low, medium, or high"
flag: --evidence (string) default="" usage="evidence signal: sufficient, insufficient, or conflicting"
flag: --host-effort (string) default="" usage="effort reported by the host: none, low, medium, high, xhigh, max"
flag: --host-model (string) default="" usage="model reported by the host; an unreplaced <placeholder> is ignored"
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="emit JSON"
flag: --message (string) default="" usage="message to render after the label"
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="mission id; records and reuses the level in .strategist/memory"
flag: --provider (string) default="" usage="ranked provider used to complete a missing host value (optional)"
flag: --reason (string) default="" usage="record a new tuple with this reason (for example escalated)"
flag: --risk (string) default="" usage="risk signal: low, medium, or high"
flag: --role (string) default="ranger" usage="role: scout, ranger, archivist, sniper, gate, or transport"
flag: --run (string) default="" usage="run id for a repeated role in one mission (for example a revision loop); each run keeps its own level"
flag: --scope (string) default="" usage="scope signal: bounded or cross_module"
flag: --width (int) default="0" usage="measured terminal width; 0 (unmeasurable) selects the stacked layout"

== strategist leveling suggest
use: suggest
short: Suggest a model and effort for a role
flag: --ambiguity (string) default="" usage="ambiguity signal"
flag: --architectural-change (bool) default="false" usage="mark an architectural change"
flag: --conflicting-evidence (bool) default="false" usage="mark conflicting evidence"
flag: --evidence (string) default="" usage="evidence signal"
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="emit JSON"
flag: --provider (string) default="CODEX" usage="ranked provider identifier"
flag: --repeated-failures (int) default="0" usage="number of repeated failures"
flag: --risk (string) default="" usage="risk signal"
flag: --role (string) default="ranger" usage="Strategist role"
flag: --scope (string) default="" usage="scope signal"
flag: --security-sensitive (bool) default="false" usage="mark a security-sensitive task"

== strategist leveling validate
use: validate
short: Validate the customer LEVELING policy
flag: --expected-digest (string) default="" usage="fail if the normalized policy digest differs"

== strategist mechanisms
use: mechanisms
short: Inspect the Mechanisms registry

== strategist mechanisms brief
use: brief --role <role>
short: Print the Tools, Mechanisms, and Feats available to one role
long: |
  Prints the role-scoped view of the Mechanisms registry
  (contracts/machine/mechanisms.yaml): what each tool is and how to invoke it.
  Roles run it from their on_start hook so an agent in a mission knows what is at
  its disposal. --stage narrows the view to a canonical Stage and its phases.
  --full adds the enforcement tier and when to use each tool.
flag: --full (bool) default="false" usage="include enforcement and when-to-use detail"
flag: --role (string) default="" usage="role to print the brief for (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --stage (string) default="" usage="canonical Stage to scope awareness to (FULL, SHORT, or ROSTER)"

== strategist metrics
use: metrics
short: Report metrics computed from Strategist's own runtime memory
long: |
  Report metrics computed from .strategist/memory/*.jsonl history. Each subcommand covers one metrics domain.

== strategist metrics confidence
use: confidence
short: Report cross-agent confidence metrics
flag: --declared (string) default="" usage="compare the claims a handoff declared with the persisted records: \"-\" reads a YAML document with a top-level confidence_summary from standard input (requires --mission; read-only)"
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="scope the review to one mission (used at the Approval Gate)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist metrics gate-outcome
use: gate-outcome
short: Record the human Approval Gate outcome as ground truth
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="mission id (required)"
flag: --outcome (string) default="" usage="accepted | revision_requested | rejected (required)"
flag: --ref (string) default="" usage="gate event that recorded the human decision (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist metrics handoff
use: handoff
short: Report Handoff Challenge governance metrics
long: |
  Report Handoff Challenge governance metrics from .strategist/memory/handoff-challenges.jsonl.
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist metrics handoff-record
use: handoff-record
short: Record the Archivist's handoff metrics line for a mission
long: |
  Append the Archivist's per-refinement line to .strategist/memory/handoff-metrics.jsonl. Only the values passed are recorded; every other field is null (an unset --reopens is null, not 0), and the two ratios are never derived because the contracts do not define them. A mission that already has a line for the same revision is left unchanged; --revision <n> records one further line per gate revision.
flag: --brief-compression-ratio (float64) default="0" usage="brief compression ratio, as measured by the caller (omit when not measured)"
flag: --brief-tokens (int64) default="0" usage="tokens in the discovery brief (omit when not measured)"
flag: --discovery-tokens (int64) default="0" usage="tokens spent by discovery (omit when not measured)"
flag: --effort (string) default="" usage="Archivist effort (omit when unknown)"
flag: --evidence-coverage-ratio (float64) default="0" usage="evidence coverage ratio, as measured by the caller (omit when not measured)"
flag: --level-source (string) default="" usage="how the level was resolved, for example host (omit when unknown)"
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="mission id (required)"
flag: --model (string) default="" usage="Archivist model (omit when unknown)"
flag: --reopens (int) default="0" usage="sources the Archivist reopened, each with a declared reason (omit when not measured; 0 means measured, none)"
flag: --revision (int) default="0" usage="gate revision number this line records (omit for the base line; one line is kept per revision)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist metrics label
use: label
short: Record a reviewed ground-truth label for a mission
flag: --kind (string) default="" usage="user_revision | handoff_validation | downstream_verification (required)"
flag: --label (string) default="" usage="reviewed outcome for the subject (required)"
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="mission id the label applies to (required)"
flag: --ref (string) default="" usage="review, event or check that decided the outcome (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --subject (string) default="" usage="route | handoff_application (required)"

