flag: --max-records (int) default="2000" usage="maximum records kept by --rotate"
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="scope the report to one mission"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --rotate (bool) default="false" usage="compact the ledger first"

== strategist metrics mission-quality
use: mission-quality
short: Evaluate the mission_quality predicates over a decisions/evidence document
long: |
  Read a YAML document from standard input (decisions, evidence, acceptance_criteria, and optionally previously_open_decision_ids and approved_scope_prefixes) and report each mission_quality predicate. The result is advisory: a failed predicate is reported and the command still exits 0. The command reads no mission artifact on its own; the caller supplies the ledger and the evidence it cites.
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="mission id (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist metrics record
use: record
short: Record a confidence claim or an explicit missing-record for a boundary
flag: --agent (string) default="" usage="producing agent (required)"
flag: --claim-file (string) default="" usage="YAML document holding one claim: or a claims: list, with its evidence: list; \"-\" reads it from standard input (preferred: no file is created), and a file inside the workspace base_path is rejected"
flag: --correlation-key (string) default="" usage="boundary correlation key (with --missing)"
flag: --missing (bool) default="false" usage="record an explicit missing-record instead of a claim"
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="mission id (required)"
flag: --reason (string) default="" usage="why no summary was produced (with --missing)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --run (string) default="" usage="optional explicit run id for a repeated role execution"

