== strategist mission normalize-openspec
use: normalize-openspec
short: Publish a completed OpenSpec change into the refined mission package
long: |
  Validates a private OpenSpec change and atomically promotes its proposal,
  design, tasks, and the mission analysis into <base_path>/refined/<mission_id>.
  OpenSpec specs and archive history remain private provider scratch.
flag: --amend (bool) default="false" usage="amend an already published package with a new change instead of publishing (analysis.md, the mission status and the original provider_change_id are kept; the previous files are snapshotted under .amendments/)"
flag: --amends (string) default="" usage="with --amend: the change being amended (the package's provider_change_id, or the previous amendment's change id)"
flag: --authorization-ref (string) default="" usage="with --amend: the human authorization for the amendment (a quote or a gate event), recorded verbatim"
flag: --change-id (string) default="" usage="completed OpenSpec change id (required)"
flag: --handoff-facts (string) default="" usage="YAML file with the typed handoff_policy_facts mapping, written into the published analysis.md frontmatter so `handoff evaluate` can derive the policy (publication only; an amendment keeps analysis.md byte-identical)"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="canonical Strategist mission id (required)"
flag: --pending-analysis (string) default="" usage="pending analysis path (default: <base_path>/pending/<mission-id>-analysis.md)"
flag: --reason (string) default="" usage="with --amend: correction rationale recorded in amendment lineage"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --runtime-root (string) default="" usage="OpenSpec runtime root (default: <strategist-root>/openspec)"
flag: --supersedes-mission-id (string) default="" usage="with --amend: prior mission id this lineage supersedes, recorded for audit"

== strategist mission observe-usage
use: observe-usage
short: Record the usage a host wrote in its own session file for one time window (opt-in, numbers only)
long: |
  strategist mission observe-usage reads a session file that Claude Code or Codex
  already wrote, for the file(s) you name with --transcript, and records the
  token counters the host itself logged inside the window [--since, --until).
  
  It is opt-in per run and never scans a home directory. The reader keeps only
  ids, timestamps, model names and numeric counters; conversation content is
  read past and never stored, printed or logged. Quality is host_measured, never
  provider_measured. Claude Code responses are deduplicated by message id and
  sub-agent files next to the transcript are included; Codex uses the delta of
  its cumulative counter. Input includes cached input; the cache part is kept
  in its own field.
  
  Attribution is by time window only. The same host session and window is
  counted once even if re-run; a re-run that sees different counts is a
  conflict, because the host file can lag the live conversation. A window with
  no host calls records nothing (never zero). The formats are not contracts:
  an unrecognized shape fails closed.
flag: --dry-run (bool) default="false" usage="print what would be recorded without writing the ledger"
flag: --host (string) default="" usage="host that wrote the file (required): claude or codex"
flag: --include-subagents (bool) default="true" usage="claude: also read <transcript>/subagents/*.jsonl"
flag: --invocation-id (string) default="" usage="the 'mission invoke' request id the window belongs to, when known"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission_id to record usage against (required)"
flag: --phase (string) default="" usage="phase the window belongs to (required)"
flag: --role (string) default="" usage="role that consumed the tokens (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --session-id (string) default="" usage="host session id when the file does not carry one"
flag: --since (string) default="" usage="window start, RFC 3339, inclusive (required)"
flag: --transcript (stringSlice) default="[]" usage="session file to read (required, repeatable)"
flag: --until (string) default="" usage="window end, RFC 3339, exclusive (required)"

== strategist mission report-usage
use: report-usage
short: Record one token usage observation for a mission phase, declared by the invoking agent
long: |
  strategist mission report-usage records ONE observation of token usage for a
  mission, declared by the LLM agent (e.g. Claude Code) that invoked this CLI.
  
  This binary never calls an LLM API and cannot verify the numbers: every record
  is stored as reported_unverified (or as an explicit estimate with
  --source estimator). It never claims provider_measured or host_measured; those
  qualities need an adapter that observes a provider or host counter itself.
  
  Report each observation once, with the counts of that call alone (an
  incremental record). Never report a running total as incremental: either use
  --record-kind cumulative_snapshot with --session-id, so only the delta between
  two snapshots of the same session is counted, or report the call's own counts.
  Pass --invocation-id (the request id printed by 'mission invoke') or --event-id
  so a repeated delivery is recognised and counted once; without one the record is
  accepted but flagged dedup_unavailable. Omit a --tokens-* flag you did not
  observe: unobserved is never recorded as zero.
  
  The command is refused until the mission has a pending, refined or archived
  artifact; report earlier invocations afterwards with an explicit --phase.
  The Approval Gate carries no tokens; use --phase unattributed for consumption
  outside any phase. Records are appended to
  .strategist/memory/mission-usage.jsonl and read by 'strategist mission usage'.
flag: --attempt (int) default="1" usage="attempt of the invocation; a real retry that consumed tokens is a new attempt"
flag: --event-id (string) default="" usage="caller-chosen idempotency key when there is no invocation id"
flag: --invocation-id (string) default="" usage="the 'mission invoke' request id (inv_...) this usage belongs to; makes the record idempotent"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission_id to record usage against (required) — must have a pending/refined/archived artifact"
flag: --model (string) default="" usage="model that served the call, when known"
flag: --phase (string) default="" usage="phase the usage belongs to (required): bootstrap, intake, discovery, refinement, execution or unattributed"
flag: --phase-run-id (string) default="" usage="phase run (r1, r2, ...) the usage belongs to, when known"
flag: --provider (string) default="" usage="provider that served the call, when known"
flag: --quality (string) default="" usage="claimed quality, never stronger than --source allows (default: reported_unverified, or heuristic_estimated for an estimator)"
flag: --record-kind (string) default="incremental" usage="incremental (this call's own counts) or cumulative_snapshot (a running total, needs --session-id)"
flag: --role (string) default="" usage="role that consumed the tokens (required): scout, ranger, archivist, sniper, shell, ..."
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --scope (string) default="invocation" usage="what the counts cover: invocation, session, phase, ..."
flag: --session-id (string) default="" usage="session of a cumulative counter; deltas are only taken inside one session"
flag: --source (string) default="agent_report" usage="origin of the numbers: agent_report or estimator"
flag: --tokens-cache (int64) default="0" usage="cache tokens the provider reported; stored separately, never added to the total"
flag: --tokens-in (int64) default="0" usage="input tokens observed for this call (omit when not observed)"
flag: --tokens-out (int64) default="0" usage="output tokens observed for this call (omit when not observed)"
flag: --tokens-reasoning (int64) default="0" usage="reasoning tokens the provider reported; stored separately, never added to the total"

