== strategist mission usage
use: usage
short: Show per-phase lifecycle and token usage for one mission (read-only)
long: |
  Show start, end, duration, runs and status per phase for one mission, with the quality of every number stated. Unobserved values print as an unavailable marker, never as zero. The legacy provider-reported ledger is shown on its own row, outside any total.
flag: --details (bool) default="false" usage="list every phase run and the legacy usage records"
flag: --from-events (string) default="" usage="rebuild the report from an exported event stream (JSONL) instead of the ledgers"
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="emit strategist-mission-usage/v1 JSON"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission identifier (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --timeline (bool) default="false" usage="add the merged chronology of lifecycle markers and usage observations"

== strategist mission verify-telemetry
use: verify-telemetry
short: Check the integrity of a mission's lifecycle and usage evidence (read-only)
long: |
  Cross-check the mission lifecycle ledger, the usage ledger and, with --events, an exported JSONL event stream (STRATEGIST_TELEMETRY_JSONL). Findings are errors (the evidence contradicts itself), warnings (a gap or a degradation) or info. The command is advisory and independent of any governance provider.
flag: --events (string) default="" usage="exported event stream (JSONL) to cross-check against the ledgers"
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="emit strategist-telemetry-verify/v1 JSON"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission identifier (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist mission view
use: view
short: Render a read-only mission experience view
long: |
  Render lifecycle, roles, advisory confidence, Approval Gate outcome, and LEVELING provenance for one mission. This command never authorizes or advances a mission.
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="emit strategist-mission-view/v1 JSON"
flag: --mission-id (string) default="" usage="mission identifier (required)"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --run (string) default="" usage="select one explicit repeated role run"

== strategist plugins
use: plugins
short: Inspect and evaluate Strategist plugin enforcement

== strategist plugins acquire-remote
use: acquire-remote
short: Acquire a pinned Git Skill-for-Hire package into quarantine
long: |
  Fetches one full-commit Git reference into an isolated temporary
  quarantine, validates the package shape and writes acquisition.json plus READY.
  It never writes external-skills-source, .strategist, the embedded catalog or a
  lockfile. Promotion remains a separate, reviewed operator action.
  Network access is opt-in and tests should omit --allow-network.
flag: --allow-network (bool) default="false" usage="explicitly authorize the Git fetch"
flag: --commit (string) default="" usage="full 40-character lowercase commit SHA (required)"
flag: --package-id (string) default="" usage="package ID expected for the imported skill (required)"
flag: --quarantine-root (string) default="" usage="optional quarantine parent; must be outside the workspace"
flag: --repository (string) default="" usage="Git repository URI or absolute local fixture path (required)"
flag: --source (string) default="git" usage="remote source class (only git is supported)"

== strategist plugins authorize
use: authorize
short: Compose authorization evidence for a governed target
long: |
  Evaluates runtime readiness, persisted Role→Weapon bindings, the two
  independent execution gates, and candidate write-target enforcement. The
  command does not invoke external providers or intercept writes performed
  outside the CLI. Use --json for stable machine-readable evidence.
flag: --approval-gate (string) default="pending" usage="Strategist Approval Gate state: pending, accepted, denied, or revision"
flag: --execution-gate (string) default="allowed" usage="local execution gate state: allowed or blocked"
flag: --json (bool) default="false" usage="print the versioned machine-readable authorization report"
flag: --mission (string) default="" usage="mission identifier to include in the report"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --target (string) default="" usage="candidate write path relative to the project root (required)"

== strategist plugins evaluate-write
use: evaluate-write
short: Report whether a write to --target is enforceably allowed under the active connector
long: |
  Classifies --target against the mission's active.yaml base_path
  (internal/plugins/policy.ClassifyWriteTarget), then checks that
  classification against the native runtime connector's own enforcement
  observation (internal/plugins/policy.EvaluateWrite).
  
  This is a scriptable, deterministic tool an agent embodying Sniper can
  invoke before writing, rather than relying only on the write_scope/
  approved_scope prose in roles/sniper.yaml — see
  .analysis/refined/20260830-skill-gaps-triage/analysis.md Cluster 1 (K03) and
  .analysis/refined/20260830-skill-gaps-followup/tasks.md item A4 for why a
  CLI-exposed check, not internal Go interception, is the right shape here:
  Sniper is a parent-agent-embodied native role, not a Go writer this binary
  can intercept.
  
  Exits non-zero when the write is not enforceably allowed, so callers can
  gate on it directly.
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --target (string) default="" usage="candidate write path to evaluate, relative to the project root (required)"

== strategist plugins prepare-embedded
use: prepare-embedded
short: Ingest external-skills-source/ into the embedded plugin catalog
long: |
  Resolves every ORKA-shaped package under --source (each subdirectory
  paired with a strategist.yaml project-adapter sidecar declaring
  canonical_role/risk_score), verifies it, and merges the result into
  internal/embed/defaults/plugins/catalog.yaml and the committed provenance
  lock. Generation-2 embedded payloads do not include generated
  skills/<id>/skill.yaml compatibility mirrors.
  
  This is a maintainer/CI operation on this repository's own embedded
  defaults (ADR-0032's pre-build ingestion pattern, generalized from Treasure
  Chest to role-slot skills — see
  .analysis/refined/20260913-embedded-skill-directory-catalog). It is not a
  per-workspace end-user command and does not touch .strategist/.
  
  Use --check in CI to fail non-zero on drift instead of writing.
flag: --check (bool) default="false" usage="fail non-zero on drift instead of writing (for CI)"
flag: --defaults-root (string) default="internal/embed/defaults" usage="internal/embed/defaults root to generate catalog.yaml and versioned skill payloads into"
flag: --lock (string) default="external-skills-source.lock.yaml" usage="path to the committed embedded-skill lock file"
flag: --source (string) default="external-skills-source" usage="directory of ORKA-shaped skill packages to ingest"

== strategist plugins resolved-digest
use: resolved-digest
short: Report whether a resolved Weapon file matches its catalog pin
long: |
  Compares a Weapon's upstream_content_digest pin (internal/embed/defaults/
  plugins/catalog.yaml) with a resolved digest — either a value already
  computed by the caller (--resolved-digest, e.g. from a Ranger handoff's
  weapon_invocation.resolved_digest) or a file this command hashes itself
  (--file, sha256 of its raw bytes). It reads only; it never invokes the
  Weapon and an unavailable pin is reported as pin_unavailable, never as a
  match (see contracts/narrative/03-discovery.md § Weapon Profile for a
  Delegated Ranger and design.md DEC-301/DEC-302 of the mission above).
  
  Exits non-zero on a mismatch, so callers can gate on it directly. A missing
  or unavailable pin, or a caller that supplied no digest, exits 0 and reports
  the status: this command answers "what do we know", not "is this Weapon
  trusted".
flag: --catalog (string) default="internal/embed/defaults/plugins/catalog.yaml" usage="path to the embedded plugin catalog"
flag: --file (string) default="" usage="path to a resolved Weapon file to hash and compare (mutually exclusive with --resolved-digest)"
flag: --provider (string) default="" usage="Weapon id to look up in the catalog (required)"
flag: --resolved-digest (string) default="" usage="an already-computed sha256:<64 hex> digest to compare (mutually exclusive with --file)"

== strategist plugins scaffold-sidecar
use: scaffold-sidecar <package-dir>
short: Generate a package's strategist.yaml sidecar deterministically
long: |
  Generates <package-dir>/strategist.yaml from the operator's declaration and
  the package (ADR-0061). --role and --slot are required and are the human
  confirmation; they are never inferred. version comes from SKILL.md
  metadata.version, or from --version when the package declares none; risk_score, category and the ranger weapon_contract are
  derived by fixed rules. upstream_* and license are filled only from an explicit
  --provenance file. openspec_root additionally needs the package's runtime/
  bundle, runtime.lock.yaml and a runtime: block in the provenance file.
  
  An existing sidecar is never overwritten without --force. --check writes
  nothing and fails non-zero when the file is missing or differs from the
  regenerated one. The command touches only <package-dir>/strategist.yaml.
flag: --check (bool) default="false" usage="fail non-zero on drift instead of writing (for CI)"
flag: --default (bool) default="false" usage="mark the Weapon as the default for its slot"
flag: --force (bool) default="false" usage="overwrite an existing, differing sidecar"
flag: --provenance (string) default="" usage="explicit provenance file supplying upstream_*, license and the openspec_root runtime block"
flag: --role (stringArray) default="[]" usage="Role the Weapon serves (repeatable, required)"
flag: --runtime (string) default="embedded" usage="runtime kind: embedded or openspec_root"
flag: --slot (stringArray) default="[]" usage="slot the Weapon supports (repeatable, required)"
flag: --version (string) default="" usage="package version, used only when SKILL.md carries no metadata.version"

== strategist provider
use: provider
short: Validate and onboard local Strategist providers

== strategist provider add
use: add <source> --slot <slot>
short: Stage and bind a validated local provider
flag: --format (string) default="table" usage="output format: table, json, or yaml"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"
flag: --slot (string) default="" usage="target slot: discovery, refinement or execution"

== strategist provider validate
use: validate <source>
short: Validate a local provider package without changing workspace state
flag: --format (string) default="table" usage="output format: table, json, or yaml"

== strategist runbook
use: runbook
short: Operate on the typed docs/runbooks/*.runbook.yaml corpus
persistent: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist runbook select
use: select
short: Select applicable runbooks for the given mission signals
long: |
  Scores docs/runbooks/*.runbook.yaml sidecars against mission signals via
  internal/feats/select_runbook.Select(), bounded by
  internal/feats/select_runbook.DefaultSelectionPolicy()
  (at most one primary, at most two supporting runbooks, each with a non-empty
  match reason). This is the select_runbook ability's concrete implementation
  (see .strategist/roles/ranger.yaml#canonical.select_runbook and
  contracts/narrative/03-discovery.md § Retrieval Cascade, stage 6).
  
  Prints an empty-result message (exit 0) when no runbook sidecar exists yet,
  or when none match the given signals — neither case is an error.
flag: --format (string) default="table" usage="output format: table or json"
flag: --signal (stringArray) default="[]" usage="mission signal to match against runbook applies_when entries (repeatable; at least one required)"

== strategist sync-governance
use: sync-governance
short: Sync .strategist/skill.yaml with explicitly provisioned governance
long: |
  Reads the explicitly selected governance directory and reconciles .strategist/skill.yaml.
  
  Checks performed:
    - Reads the source metadata to verify the governance fingerprint
    - Reads source/governance-core.json to extract active mandates
    - Compares active mandates against compliance.mandates in skill.yaml
    - Applies missing governance fields (validation_policy, budget_policy, telemetry_policy)
    - Reports drift before applying changes
  
  Use --dry-run to preview changes without writing.
flag: --dry-run (bool) default="false" usage="preview changes without writing"
flag: --governance-dir (string) default="" usage="path to the explicitly provisioned governance directory"
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist treasure-chest
use: treasure-chest
short: Show treasure chest runtime status and index health
long: |
  Show the current treasure chest configuration, governance, index, and compiled artifact status.
  
  Default: read-only status view. Merges four runtime truth layers:
    - .strategist/active.yaml         (configured/scoped chests)
    - .strategist/treasure-chests.yaml (governed trust and routing policy)
    - .strategist/knowledge.index.yaml (indexed retrieval sources)
    - .strategist/.compiled/.index.gz  (compiled fast-path artifact)
  
  Use --index to rebuild the compiled knowledge index from declared sources.
  Use --include-historical with --index to opt in to indexing T2/T3 sources.
flag: --format (string) default="table" usage="output format: table or json"
flag: --include-historical (bool) default="false" usage="include T2/T3 historical sources in index rebuild (requires --index)"
flag: --index (bool) default="false" usage="rebuild compiled knowledge index from declared sources"
flag: --scope (string) default="" usage="filter output by slot scope (e.g. discovery, refinement, execution)"
persistent: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: auto-discovered from CWD)"

== strategist treasure-chest add
use: add <path>
short: Register a new treasure chest across active/governed/indexed layers
long: |
  Add a treasure chest source, updating active.yaml, treasure-chests.yaml, and
  knowledge.index.yaml together in one pass. Existing file comments/formatting are preserved.
  
  Leaves the compiled index (.compiled/.index.gz) stale unless --index is also passed.
flag: --id (string) default="" usage="chest id (default: derived from the last path segment)"
flag: --index (bool) default="false" usage="rebuild the compiled index immediately after adding"
flag: --reviewed-by (string) default="human" usage="who reviewed this source"
flag: --scope (string) default="all" usage="slot Scope: all, discovery, refinement, or execution"
flag: --tags (string) default="" usage="comma-separated task_type tags (default: all)"
flag: --trust-tier (string) default="T1" usage="trust tier: T0, T1, T2, or T3"

== strategist treasure-chest doctor
use: doctor
short: Detect consistency drift across active.yaml, treasure-chests.yaml, and knowledge.index.yaml
long: |
  Read-only diagnostic for treasure-chest add/remove consistency.
  
  Reports chests present in one of the three registry truth layers
  (active.yaml, treasure-chests.yaml, knowledge.index.yaml) but missing from
  another — the divergence a batch write failure can leave behind.
  
  Detection only: no automatic repair is attempted. Exits non-zero when any
  divergence is found.

== strategist treasure-chest index
use: index
short: Rebuild the offline knowledge substrate (scan, propose jewels, refresh compiled index)
long: |
  Rebuild the offline knowledge substrate from declared sources and mission history.
  
  Responsibilities:
    - Validate configured, governed, indexed, and compiled layers.
    - Run the internal scan phase over <base_path>/refined/**/tasks.md and <base_path>/done/**.
    - Detect and polish reusable knowledge units into deduplicated status:proposed jewels.
    - Rebuild the compiled knowledge index (.strategist/.compiled/.index.gz).
  
  Use --include-historical to opt in to indexing T2/T3 sources into the compiled artifact.
flag: --include-historical (bool) default="false" usage="include T2/T3 historical sources in the compiled index rebuild"

== strategist treasure-chest items
use: items
short: Inspect and curate jewels and potions regardless of curation status

== strategist treasure-chest items accept
use: accept <item-id>...
short: Promote item ids to status: accepted

== strategist treasure-chest items check-evidence
use: check-evidence <chest-id>
short: Advisory scan for expired, duplicate, or conflicting jewels in a chest
long: |
  Runs three advisory checks over a chest's non-deprecated jewels:
    expired    — valid_until has passed
    duplicate  — same normalized statement (trimmed, case-folded)
    conflict   — overlapping source_refs with a differing statement or status
  
  Never modifies a jewel. Always exits 0, regardless of findings — same
  advisory-only posture as mission_quality, not a CI gate.

== strategist treasure-chest items deprecate
use: deprecate <item-id>...
short: Mark item ids as status: deprecated

== strategist treasure-chest items list
use: list
short: List items (jewels and/or potions), optionally filtered by kind, status, or chest
long: |
  Lists items across all chests.
  
  Without --status: shows proposed, accepted, and verified items (everything "alive").
  deprecated items are excluded unless --status=all or --status=deprecated is given.
  Without --kind: shows both jewels and potions.
flag: --chest (string) default="" usage="filter by chest id"
flag: --format (string) default="table" usage="output format: table or json"
flag: --kind (string) default="" usage="filter by item kind: jewel or potion (default: both)"
flag: --status (string) default="" usage="filter by status: all, proposed, accepted, verified, or deprecated (default: all except deprecated)"

== strategist treasure-chest items migrate-status
use: migrate-status
short: One-time migration: rewrite legacy status: active jewels to status: accepted

== strategist treasure-chest items show
use: show <item-id>
short: Show a single item's (jewel or potion) full content
flag: --format (string) default="table" usage="output format: table or json"

== strategist treasure-chest items verify
use: verify <item-id>...
short: Promote item ids to status: verified (requires --evidence)
flag: --evidence (string) default="" usage="evidence reference recorded with verify (jewels only — see PromotePotion)"

== strategist treasure-chest list
use: list
short: Show treasure chest runtime status (explicit name for the default view)
flag: --format (string) default="table" usage="output format: table or json"
flag: --scope (string) default="" usage="filter output by slot scope (e.g. discovery, refinement, execution)"

== strategist treasure-chest remove
use: remove [path]
short: Tombstone a treasure chest (mark inactive, do not hard-delete)
long: |
  Remove a treasure chest from active.yaml's active declarations and mark it
  status: inactive in treasure-chests.yaml and knowledge.index.yaml, preserving an audit
  trail instead of hard-deleting the entry. Resolve by positional path or --id; if both are
  given and disagree, the command stops with an ambiguity error.
flag: --id (string) default="" usage="chest id to remove (alternative to positional path)"

== strategist treasure-chest scan
use: scan
hidden: true
short: [internal] Mine .analysis/refined and .analysis/done for recurring clusters and open gaps
long: |
  Internal phase folded into "strategist treasure-chest index" — not part of the
  public steady-state UX. Kept as a standalone command for debugging/dry-run inspection of
  the scan phase in isolation.
  
  Scan mission history for recurring themes and unresolved side quests.
  
  Input: <base_path>/refined/**/tasks.md and <base_path>/done/** only. Never reads
  <base_path>/pending/ or <base_path>/archived/ reports.
  
  Method: lexical/tag matching only. No embeddings, no vector index.
  
  Output: .strategist/treasure/clusters/ and .strategist/treasure/gaps/, regenerated from
  scratch on every run (safe to delete — see docs/configuration.md § Storage Domain).
  
  Use --dry-run to preview output without writing to disk.
flag: --dry-run (bool) default="false" usage="print what would be written without touching disk"

== strategist upgrade
use: upgrade
short: Reconcile an installed .strategist/ runtime against the current embedded defaults
long: |
  Reconcile an installed .strategist/ runtime against the current embedded
  defaults across the full runtime tree (unlike a plain "strategist install",
  which only re-applies the small set of strictly-guarded normative files).
  
  Every file is classified before anything is written:
    managed      matches the current embedded default already — no-op
    missing      part of current defaults, absent on disk — written
    auto_upgrade on disk, matches what was last installed, embedded moved on — written
    customized   on disk, diverges from what was last installed — preserved unless --force
    orphaned     tracked by a prior install, no longer part of current defaults — reported, never deleted
  
  Use --dry-run to see the plan without writing anything. Any file upgrade
  overwrites (auto_upgrade, or customized with --force) is snapshotted first
  under .strategist/.upgrade-backups/<timestamp>/ — restore it with
  "strategist upgrade --rollback <timestamp>" (or --rollback latest).
flag: --allow-downgrade (bool) default="false" usage="let this binary replace normative files installed by a newer binary (deliberate rollback; default: refuse with runtime_newer_than_binary)"
flag: --dry-run (bool) default="false" usage="show the upgrade plan without writing anything"
flag: --force (bool) default="false" usage="also overwrite customized files (default: preserve them)"
flag: --global (bool) default="false" usage="operate on the global root (default: local project)"
flag: --rollback (string) default="" usage="restore files from a previous upgrade's backup instead of upgrading (\"latest\" or a specific timestamp from .strategist/.upgrade-backups/)"
flag: --target (string) default="" usage="target repository root (default: current directory)"

== strategist validate
use: validate
short: Validate the .strategist/ configuration tree
long: |
  Validate all configuration files inside a .strategist/ directory.
  
  Checks performed:
    - active.yaml: exists, valid YAML, required fields (mode, base_path, slots)
    - personas/*.yaml: each has tone_directive and phase_labels
    - roles/*.yaml: each has discovery, refinement, execution slots
    - knowledge.index.yaml: if present, valid YAML
flag: --root (string) default="" usage="path to .strategist/ root (default: .strategist)"

== strategist version
use: version
short: Print the strategist version
flag: --build (bool) default="false" usage="also print the commit, platform and embedded OpenSpec runtime of this binary"

